Add :mod:`icalendar.itip`, a receiving-side iTIP state machine for REQUEST and CANCEL messages. It merges meeting components by UID, ORGANIZER and RECURRENCE-ID, orders updates with SEQUENCE and DTSTAMP, keeps cancellations as versioned tombstones so late stale messages cannot revive a meeting, reports applied/ignored/conflict per message, and serializes to JSON. REPLY, COUNTER and RANGE=THISANDFUTURE are rejected; sender authentication stays with the caller.
